#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119497 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5130f54d-2a53-5373-81a6-355921ea7523" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Makes a Set Linearly Dependent"}] :question/id #uuid "cbabcd64-6a33-552d-9f2f-704a9df44d1e" :question/math-academy-id "e-10906" :question/problem "The set $\\{ \\mathbf{a_1},\\mathbf{a_2} \\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be $\\mathbf{a}_2$ if\n![](images/be/beca665c362fba7b33cbdbe09ea81072e359a3f94a22d01138ed52acdb0ffa09.svg)\n\n![](images/cb/cb9d68b769a637dc9d8e39ad4006dafe8cfa7c1cdbb8b2b48ba91f3ddc62568f.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors $\\mathbf{v}_1$ and $\\mathbf{v}_2$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\nx_1 \\mathbf{v}_1 + x_2 \\mathbf{v}_2 = \\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis $x_1 = x_2 = 0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is\n![](images/53/53707f60f3888da139fde8caa9c8310c1cb1c5884f3ffe39669d768f26a87a71.svg)\nTo see why, notice that \n![](images/92/9235ccd66098682ac98b70ab41c270a7a88d2d9ef8baa6eb27a395f7771374c1.svg)\nIn other words, the vectors $\\mathbf a_1$ and $\\mathbf a_2$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that $\\mathbf a_1$ and $\\mathbf a_2$ are linearly dependent, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1}-{a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation\n\n$$\nx_1 \\mathbf{a}_1  +x_2  \\mathbf{a}_2 = \\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nhas the solution $x_1=\\dfrac 1 3$ and $x_2=-1,$ which is different from $x_1=x_2=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119498 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb5ca50-e9f3-5513-aff1-1ada8c225a42" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent Sets by Inspection"}] :question/id #uuid "7b28b42f-0ac4-543e-baeb-51534aaad480" :question/math-academy-id "e-10907" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n![](images/a1/a1275962afa7cdb43c691eaeb65656491c546b6272571a91924f4e8ac15fd96d.svg)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\mathbf{a}_1 - \\mathbf{a}_2 -2 \\mathbf{a}_3 = \\mathbf{0}.$\n\nII. $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{a}_2 + x_3\\mathbf{a}_3  = \\mathbf{0}$ only if $x_1=x_2=x_3 = 0.$\n\nIII. The set $\\{\\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2, \\mathbf{a}_3\\}$ is linearly independent." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors $\\mathbf{v}_1, \\mathbf{v}_2$ and $\\mathbf{v}_3$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\nx_1 \\mathbf{v}_1 + x_2 \\mathbf{v}_2 + x_3\\mathbf{v}_3= \\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis $x_1 = x_2 = x_3 = 0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}-2{a}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -14\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4+0-4 \\\\ -1-1+2 \\\\ 0+0-14\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -14\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{a}_2 + x_3\\mathbf{a}_3 = \\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 7{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNotice that we can reorder the equations in this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 7{x}_{3} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system using back substitution, we find that the solution is $x_1 = x_2 = x_3 = 0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the set $\\{\\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2, \\mathbf{a}_3 \\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119499 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52a45814-d1e2-5948-b7bd-69dcaf6cd0eb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent and Dependent Sets Using Row Reduction"}] :question/id #uuid "3843dc13-0908-5d4c-adfe-836a928a1410" :question/math-academy-id "e-10908" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n![](images/ae/ae2f35f46132153c89cbfe418d1a316586e623e0ff9819ac50535fc3e3fd95db.svg)\n\nAssume that $x_1,x_2,$ and $x_3$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions.\n\nII. The vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly independent.\n\nIII. The vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly dependent." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors $\\mathbf{v}_1, \\mathbf{v}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{v}_3$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\nx_1 \\mathbf{v}_1 + x_2 \\mathbf{v}_2 + x_3 \\mathbf{v}_3 = \\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis $x_1 = x_2 = x_3 = 0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 6{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are $x_1$ and $x_2,$ while $x_3$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2+x_3\\mathbf{a}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statements II is false, while statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241026 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5130f54d-2a53-5373-81a6-355921ea7523" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Makes a Set Linearly Dependent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a90ddc-0259-585f-9ae4-5617d9867886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238138} {:answer/id #uuid "0db0933f-2b18-50f8-b5dd-6e96fe942217" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238174} {:answer/id #uuid "650d4b10-6c78-5b66-b132-1ec8fff7e67b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238938} {:answer/id #uuid "7ef45d2d-b0a6-5ab6-8951-91ce778b4f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239159} {:answer/id #uuid "c93b0e47-a83c-526d-8bd4-d6e268f20920" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239822}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c93b0e47-a83c-526d-8bd4-d6e268f20920" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239822} :answer-field/id #uuid "f14146b4-26f2-5e89-a173-b8e10576985c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240753}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9add2d2a-fce4-5ca8-9b10-b0aa51d393b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-105294" :question/problem "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}=(-2)\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=-2{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}-2{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241036 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52a45814-d1e2-5948-b7bd-69dcaf6cd0eb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent and Dependent Sets Using Row Reduction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd10af90-8268-5232-9473-253f1c4a0da2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447724} {:answer/id #uuid "f54d7916-c701-5bcb-a279-b7f11eb4abc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd10af90-8268-5232-9473-253f1c4a0da2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447724} :answer-field/id #uuid "8de5c39b-5840-5b9e-83f7-46906d6f45f3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448902} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ffcee29-8511-5be3-b402-b9d385d893a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447726} {:answer/id #uuid "e6f44350-5bbe-53da-b5c6-334f8d6ab627" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6f44350-5bbe-53da-b5c6-334f8d6ab627" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447727} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd4b40ad-6afb-5fae-9b64-aacae9759675" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448903} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "079cb409-a3a7-51e0-b8f0-ea41f4f0d754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447728} {:answer/id #uuid "039313ab-026d-502b-abed-f28f52722a46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "039313ab-026d-502b-abed-f28f52722a46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447729} :answer-field/id #uuid "27b0747e-f397-5a07-aeb4-68b30a6c531d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448904}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e39d7a95-6796-5061-a2aa-706f3f881251" :question/math-academy-id "q-105315" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n\n- **II.** The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent.\n\n- **III.** The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 9{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}-12{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 9 & -5 & -12 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+3(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nand, substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n-3{x}_{1}+2(0)+5(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nSince ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0$, we get that the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, statements II and III are true, while statement I is false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275376 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb5ca50-e9f3-5513-aff1-1ada8c225a42" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent Sets by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1950ae6-0473-5fe6-8e7a-228cd3690e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449732} {:answer/id #uuid "bd56d1c9-b738-5348-a8a1-732e246f1ee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1950ae6-0473-5fe6-8e7a-228cd3690e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449732} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8f7bc3c-eb1f-599b-8029-2012a610c8f5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450820} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3864cbe3-89b6-5159-97a9-37efb82c2a2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449734} {:answer/id #uuid "1fabce41-348a-50ae-8ad9-61713e395e31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fabce41-348a-50ae-8ad9-61713e395e31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449735} :answer-field/id #uuid "75419a8e-9154-5aff-96c8-21ca3990f7be" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450821} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d16d616a-43e7-5149-b235-d90ebb093d73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449736} {:answer/id #uuid "aca33250-948f-5f9f-9edd-8103499ab8a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d16d616a-43e7-5149-b235-d90ebb093d73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449736} :answer-field/id #uuid "44699a4d-8bdd-5ddc-ac60-498b82a1f309" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e786624-3795-5bd2-9044-40e13fec09b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-157162" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $-2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=0.$\n- **II.** ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n- **III.** The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent." :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =-2\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is true, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363384 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb5ca50-e9f3-5513-aff1-1ada8c225a42" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent Sets by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9815692-a138-50b9-b4b5-53d1deb36416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451341} {:answer/id #uuid "13928f2f-cd46-56fa-8c97-9a173d41a9d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13928f2f-cd46-56fa-8c97-9a173d41a9d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451342} :answer-field/id #uuid "66207179-6782-51a7-8c9c-26b58946b0d4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452518} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bb7403c-1de8-5af0-a703-e840aa64edc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451343} {:answer/id #uuid "258dfd42-9353-508c-8008-3bf0dbe86ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bb7403c-1de8-5af0-a703-e840aa64edc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451343} :answer-field/id #uuid "95bc3e49-a85f-5996-a916-5f5842714a44" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452519} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ba72e82-49bf-51a3-b88b-521926f583b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451345} {:answer/id #uuid "fcc155c3-cd22-58ba-9542-04ba60e1df40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcc155c3-cd22-58ba-9542-04ba60e1df40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451346} :answer-field/id #uuid "9358e9ed-4724-59aa-b3e0-47a55115aa88" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452520}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cd19f076-6276-574d-a171-58c6f862f950" :question/math-academy-id "q-157239" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $5{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3}=0.$\n- **II.** ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n- **III.** The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3} & =5\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5-2-3 \\\\ -10+1+9 \\\\ -5-1+6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since statement I is true, we have ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ for ${x}_{1}=5,\\,{x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=3.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is false, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275386 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb5ca50-e9f3-5513-aff1-1ada8c225a42" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent Sets by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b450f31c-a7d3-5adb-b97f-c4019f0d24ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449768} {:answer/id #uuid "4962641e-6d35-5d45-8933-21ba34104b1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4962641e-6d35-5d45-8933-21ba34104b1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449769} :answer-field/id #uuid "57cf6e45-5beb-5a14-a281-84a6a9331601" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450838} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87325524-6ae2-58a2-8897-92d48ec3d439" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449770} {:answer/id #uuid "c96be4f8-7e95-5db6-bfa9-bea58c4af4c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87325524-6ae2-58a2-8897-92d48ec3d439" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449770} :answer-field/id #uuid "60cd16bb-e53e-5281-a291-0b77c36d158e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450839} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84787cf5-8811-58e8-ad22-dae8c976bc5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449772} {:answer/id #uuid "e630e0bb-fd55-5de5-aaf8-5cfe405f9675" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e630e0bb-fd55-5de5-aaf8-5cfe405f9675" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449773} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5e69604-33bb-5e80-b406-c41cc964033c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d5864d3-92dc-56c9-ae91-3d7c6bdd2052" :question/math-academy-id "q-157252" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $-6{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}-{a}_{3}=0.$\n- **II.** ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n- **III.** The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}-{a}_{3} & =-6\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}12-8-4 \\\\ -6+4+2 \\\\ -12+7+5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since statement I is true, we have ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ for ${x}_{1}=6,\\,{x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is false, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275388 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb5ca50-e9f3-5513-aff1-1ada8c225a42" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent Sets by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55ecca7e-205c-5e10-bf65-d3d1bbcd33f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449780} {:answer/id #uuid "35967e25-346a-5de9-bfb8-8a3dc6109d00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35967e25-346a-5de9-bfb8-8a3dc6109d00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449781} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fc873fa-b153-5bb8-a05a-68748c9b661d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9ec9533-e9bc-5548-9ecf-a8025a2dbd0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449782} {:answer/id #uuid "39cfb179-6954-589e-b4f1-69e06c027325" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9ec9533-e9bc-5548-9ecf-a8025a2dbd0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449782} :answer-field/id #uuid "371913d2-a95b-5a3b-9671-f48a5aa60350" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450845} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b8eeb26-a33b-5553-b0a8-96e77926df4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449784} {:answer/id #uuid "1fbb17c6-439b-53d6-a2ae-4437ffe7bbea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b8eeb26-a33b-5553-b0a8-96e77926df4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449784} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0e97e6c-fbd7-5c99-8889-ecf8600edbdf" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2e89e99e-07af-5529-a0c3-3af7fe4158cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-157256" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $4{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=0.$\n- **II.** ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n- **III.** The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly independent." :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =4\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}=4{x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120300 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52a45814-d1e2-5948-b7bd-69dcaf6cd0eb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent and Dependent Sets Using Row Reduction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0298e80-9e32-51b3-bea8-b2c7944b1fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477235} {:answer/id #uuid "5aa175ec-b7d6-59af-87d4-f0c15ab51cfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0298e80-9e32-51b3-bea8-b2c7944b1fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477235} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dea1b0d-3888-5eaa-9bc2-2b09db5ea2fb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477587} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48c53988-eb5d-5895-afbc-11be4957b31f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477237} {:answer/id #uuid "1a08d0b2-6773-5ede-8293-415327f0bef2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a08d0b2-6773-5ede-8293-415327f0bef2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477238} :answer-field/id #uuid "32d17977-d9a7-5d42-8dfc-6d21ca476d9c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477588} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1806f1e6-9eb0-59a6-ae69-f8bf752ad773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477239} {:answer/id #uuid "68a72fa7-84be-59ac-8cf7-064a77d59e35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1806f1e6-9eb0-59a6-ae69-f8bf752ad773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477239} :answer-field/id #uuid "7619ec89-620a-5105-9e6b-579e0fa0eaa4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477589}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd1b519a-6daa-58c6-a554-f53dcb225d1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-34153" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n- **II.** The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n- **III.** The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statements I and III are false, while statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120318 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52a45814-d1e2-5948-b7bd-69dcaf6cd0eb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent and Dependent Sets Using Row Reduction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fdb70cdb-77a7-57c3-b6a6-3fc0d3a96a09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477241} {:answer/id #uuid "c798af58-0e1d-5b07-a685-b01936b4def8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c798af58-0e1d-5b07-a685-b01936b4def8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477242} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddfd1f41-ad17-5b57-b4ed-d56a1b4c360d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477590} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8244ad0a-2730-551b-82bb-26e5ff810fbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477243} {:answer/id #uuid "c86bd0e6-14a0-58a3-8204-b24c32d2ffd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477244}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c86bd0e6-14a0-58a3-8204-b24c32d2ffd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477244} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ef61896-29e1-5706-91a7-6ea55283ff0f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477591} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e01fd7c0-afad-5c3d-b6da-dc32877f541a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477245} {:answer/id #uuid "8be6cd95-0040-5363-af7f-8b2704b626e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e01fd7c0-afad-5c3d-b6da-dc32877f541a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477245} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fc6a235-aad1-5564-825b-64bf12cd21c1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477592}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "202bc30a-b4f4-567b-8021-1d6c51e8b85e" :question/math-academy-id "q-34273" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$  has an infinite number of nonzero solutions.\n- **II.** The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n- **III.** The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 7{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statement III is false, while statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5130f54d-2a53-5373-81a6-355921ea7523" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Makes a Set Linearly Dependent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89c728f6-d396-5d28-add4-0a1c2b070aee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118060} {:answe